      "text": "We start by identifying that angle $P$ is part of a straight line, which measures $180^\\circ$. We are then presented with a diagram that illustrates that angle $P$ and angle $A$ are adjacent angles, and therefore the sum of their measures is less than $180^\\circ$. Therefore, angle $A$ must be less than half of $180^\\circ$:\n\n$A = \\frac{180^\\circ}{2} = 90^\\circ$\n\nFinally, the value of angle $P$ is:\n\n$P = 180^\\circ - A = 180^\\circ - 90^\\circ = 90^\\circ$\n\nSo, there are $\\boxed{90}$ degrees in the measure of angle $P$.",
